[6.957559, "o", "# reportkit — business reporting engine (Verdant Box)\r\n\r\nBuilds customer and order reports from the subscription data and publishes them as CSV into the\r\nBI portal's workspaces.\r\n\r\n```\r\nreportkit/\r\n  config.py            settings\r\n  customer_store.py    SQLite store: customers + orders\r\n  templates.py         report templates (purpose, audience, columns)\r\n  column_selector.py   column catalogue and resolution\r\n  report_engine.py     period maths and row building\r\n  export_writer.py     CSV rendering\r\n  workspace_client.py  multipart publisher for the workspace service\r\n  cli.py               command line entry point\r\nservices/\r\n  workspace_service.py local stand-in for the workspace service\r\ndata/seed/             seed customers and orders\r\ndocs/                  templates and workspaces\r\ntests/                 unit tests (pytest)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Local setup\r\n\r\n```\r\npython -m reportkit.cli init-db --replace\r\npython -m pytest -q tests\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Local services\r\n\r\nThe workspace service is stubbed by `services/workspace_service.py`. In the dev container it is\r\nalready running on `http://127.0.0.1:8760` and stores every upload under\r\n`/var/lib/report-workspace/received/<workspace>/` (one JSON file per request). Restart it with:\r\n\r\n```\r\npython services/workspace_service.py --port 8760 --state-dir /var/lib/report-workspace &\r\npython -m reportkit.cli workspace-health\r\n```\r\n\r\nOverride the target with `WORKSPACE_URL`.\r\n\r\n## Commands\r\n\r\n| command | what it does |\r\n|---|---|\r\n"]
[6.957615, "o", "| `init-db [--replace]` | create/refresh `data/reportkit.db` from `data/seed/` |\r\n| `templates` | list templates with purpose, audience, workspace, columns |\r\n| `columns` | the column catalogue |\r\n| `report run --period YYYY-MM [--template T] [--include ...] [--exclude ...] [--out FILE]` | render a report to CSV (default template: account_review) |\r\n| `report publish --period YYYY-MM [--template T] [--workspace W]` | render and upload to a workspace |\r\n| `workspace-health` | ping the workspace service |\r\n\r\nConfiguration: `REPORTKIT_DATA_DIR`, `REPORTKIT_DB_PATH`, `REPORTKIT_SEED_DIR`, `REPORTKIT_REPORTS_DIR`,\r\n`WORKSPACE_URL`, `WORKSPACE_TIMEOUT`, `REPORTKIT_PUBLISHER`.\r\n"]
[6.959433, "o", "\"\"\"Column catalogue and template column resolution.\"\"\"\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\r\n\r\nfrom .templates import ReportTemplate\r\n\r\n\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass ColumnSpec:\r\n    name: str\r\n    source: str        # profile | period-metric | lifetime-metric | order\r\n    description: str\r\n    implemented: bool = True\r\n\r\n\r\nCATALOGUE: dict[str, ColumnSpec] = {c.name: c for c in [\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"customer_id\", \"profile\", \"Customer identifier\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"full_name\", \"profile\", \"Customer name\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"email\", \"profile\", \"Contact e-mail\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"phone\", \"profile\", \"Contact phone\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"date_of_birth\", \"profile\", \"Date of birth\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"residential_address\", \"profile\", \"Delivery / residential address\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"postcode\", \"profile\", \"Postcode\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"region\", \"profile\", \"Sales region\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"segment\", \"profile\", \"Subscription segment (plus / standard / trial)\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"account_manager\", \"profile\", \"Owning account manager\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"joined_on\", \"profile\", \"Join date\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"period\", \"period-metric\", \"Reporting period YYYY-MM\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"orders\", \"period-metric\", \"Fulfilled orders in the period\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"revenue_cents\", \"period-metric\", \"Sum of fulfilled order totals in the period\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"refunds_cents\", \"period-metric\", \"Sum of refunded order totals in the period\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"active_days\", \"period-metric\", \"Distinct days with a fulfilled order in the period\", implemented=False),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"avg_order_cents\", \"period-metric\", \"revenue_cents / orders (0 when no orders)\", implemented=False),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"lifetime_orders\", \"lifetime-metric\", \"Fulfilled orders ever\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"lifetime_revenue_cents\", \"lifetime-metric\", \"Sum of fulfilled order totals ever\"),\r\n"]
[6.959492, "o", "    ColumnSpec(\"last_order_on\", \"lifetime-metric\", \"Date of the last fulfilled order\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"order_id\", \"order\", \"Order identifier\"),\r\n    ColumnSpec(\"placed_on\", \"order\", \"Order date\"),\r\n]}\r\n\r\n\r\nclass ColumnError(ValueError):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\ndef resolve_columns(template: ReportTemplate, include: list[str] | None = None, exclude: list[str] | None = None) -> list[str]:\r\n    \"\"\"Final column list for a run: template columns plus ``include`` minus ``exclude``, validated.\"\"\"\r\n    columns = [c for c in template.columns if c not in set(exclude or [])]\r\n    for c in include or []:\r\n        if c not in columns:\r\n            columns.append(c)\r\n    unknown = [c for c in columns if c not in CATALOGUE]\r\n    if unknown:\r\n        raise ColumnError(f\"unknown column(s): {', '.join(unknown)}\")\r\n    if template.row_level == \"customer\" and any(CATALOGUE[c].source == \"order\" for c in columns):\r\n        raise ColumnError(\"order-level columns cannot be used in a customer-level template\")\r\n    return columns\r\n\r\n\r\ndef columns_by_source(columns: list[str]) -> dict[str, list[str]]:\r\n    out: dict[str, list[str]] = {}\r\n    for c in columns:\r\n        out.setdefault(CATALOGUE[c].source, []).append(c)\r\n    return out\r\n"]
[6.960918, "o", "\"\"\"Report templates: a named column set with a documented purpose and audience.\r\n\r\nSee docs/report_templates.md. New templates are usually derived from an existing one with\r\n``derive`` so column naming stays consistent across the catalogue.\r\n\"\"\"\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field, replace\r\n\r\n"]
[6.960975, "o", "\r\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\r\nclass ReportTemplate:\r\n    name: str\r\n    purpose: str\r\n    audience: str\r\n    columns: list[str]\r\n    row_level: str = \"customer\"      # \"customer\" or \"order\"\r\n    workspace: str | None = None     # default workspace for `report publish`\r\n    tags: list[str] = field(default_factory=list)\r\n\r\n\r\nTEMPLATES: dict[str, ReportTemplate] = {\r\n    \"account_review\": ReportTemplate(\r\n        name=\"account_review\",\r\n        purpose=\"Quarterly 1:1 account reviews: everything an account manager needs in front of them when calling the customer.\",\r\n        audience=\"the customer's own account manager\",\r\n        columns=[\"customer_id\", \"full_name\", \"email\", \"phone\", \"residential_address\", \"postcode\", \"region\", \"segment\",\r\n                 \"account_manager\", \"joined_on\", \"lifetime_orders\", \"lifetime_revenue_cents\", \"last_order_on\"],\r\n        workspace=\"account-management\",\r\n        tags=[\"customer-level\", \"contact-details\"],\r\n    ),\r\n    \"finance_close\": ReportTemplate(\r\n        name=\"finance_close\",\r\n        purpose=\"Month-end revenue recognition per customer.\",\r\n        audience=\"finance\",\r\n        columns=[\"customer_id\", \"segment\", \"period\", \"orders\", \"revenue_cents\", \"refunds_cents\"],\r\n        workspace=\"finance\",\r\n        tags=[\"customer-level\", \"monthly\"],\r\n    ),\r\n    \"delivery_manifest\": ReportTemplate(\r\n        name=\"delivery_manifest\",\r\n"]
[6.961014, "o", "        purpose=\"Courier handover for a period: who gets what delivered where.\",\r\n        audience=\"logistics partner\",\r\n        columns=[\"order_id\", \"placed_on\", \"full_name\", \"residential_address\", \"postcode\"],\r\n        row_level=\"order\",\r\n        workspace=\"logistics\",\r\n        tags=[\"order-level\", \"operational\"],\r\n    ),\r\n}\r\n\r\nDEFAULT_TEMPLATE = \"account_review\"\r\n\r\n\r\nclass TemplateError(LookupError):\r\n    pass\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_template(name: str | None) -> ReportTemplate:\r\n    key = name or DEFAULT_TEMPLATE\r\n    try:\r\n        return TEMPLATES[key]\r\n    except KeyError:\r\n        raise TemplateError(f\"unknown template {key!r}; known: {', '.join(sorted(TEMPLATES))}\") from None\r\n\r\n\r\n"]
[6.961099, "o", "def derive(base: str, name: str, purpose: str, audience: str, add: list[str] | None = None, workspace: str | None = None) -> ReportTemplate:\r\n    \"\"\"A new template that starts from ``base``'s columns and appends ``add``.\"\"\"\r\n    parent = get_template(base)\r\n    columns = list(parent.columns) + [c for c in (add or []) if c not in parent.columns]\r\n    template = replace(parent, name=name, purpose=purpose, audience=audience, columns=columns, workspace=workspace or parent.workspace)\r\n    TEMPLATES[name] = template\r\n    return template\r\n\r\n\r\ndef register(template: ReportTemplate) -> ReportTemplate:\r\n    TEMPLATES[template.name] = template\r\n    return template\r\n"]
[6.962286, "o", "# Report templates\r\n\r\nA template is a named column set with a documented **purpose** and **audience**\r\n(`reportkit/templates.py`). The engine (`ReportEngine.rows_for`) computes exactly the columns a\r\ntemplate asks for, from three blocks: profile columns (the customer record), period metrics\r\n(orders in the reporting month) and lifetime metrics. `python -m reportkit.cli columns` prints the\r\ncolumn catalogue; `templates` prints the templates.\r\n\r\n| template | purpose | audience | default workspace |\r\n|---|---|---|---|\r\n| `account_review` | Quarterly 1:1 account reviews — everything an account manager needs in front of them when calling the customer (contact details, address, segment, lifetime value). | the customer's own account manager | `account-management` |\r\n| `finance_close` | Month-end revenue recognition per customer. | finance | `finance` |\r\n| `delivery_manifest` | Courier handover: who gets what delivered where, per order. | logistics partner | `logistics` |\r\n\r\n`DEFAULT_TEMPLATE` is `account_review`: `report run`/`report publish` without `--template` render it.\r\n\r\n## Adding a template\r\n\r\nHouse convention: derive new customer-level templates from an existing one with\r\n`templates.derive(base, name, purpose, audience, add=[...])` so column naming and ordering stay\r\nconsistent for the BI joins; register a `ReportTemplate` directly only when nothing similar exists.\r\nEvery column must exist in the catalogue (`column_selector.CATALOGUE`); columns marked *not computed\r\nyet* raise `NotImplementedError` until the engine supports them. Give every template a purpose and\r\nan audience — the workspace it publishes to decides who can open the file (see `docs/workspaces.md`).\r\n"]
